                <pb facs="0692" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4020: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-08T13:00:00+00:00">December 8, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. John Whittaker, <hi rendition="#italic">Herald Tribune</hi> war
                    correspondent, and Miss Davis of <hi rendition="#italic">Chicago News</hi> both
                    with rebel forces since beginning, drove here from Burgos yesterday and called
                    on me last night. They report that Vitoria is threatened seriously by strong
                    well-equipped Government forces from Bilbao now within striking distance of city
                    and that Franco, alarmed, has weakened his army before Madrid by sending Moorish
                    reinforcements. The Loyalists clearly have retaken the towns between Bilbao and
                    the present position.</p>
                <p>They report that Salamanca resembles a German military camp, German officers
                    predominating. From a German officer on Madrid <pb facs="0693" n="594"
                        xml:id="pg594"/> front Whittaker heard not for publication there is much
                    irritation among German and Italian officers because Franco objects to the
                    destruction of Madrid from the air.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
